{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#4142","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#4142","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#4142\",\"parent_revision\":\"9aff1006d948858015651fcaad384ae55a103c18\",\"root_revision\":\"78561f72ec684140c03bde776d7217b298b421e714d7a3c43195b382d48ecbae\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: needs-grooming\\nadded: 2026-10-17\\n-->\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-10-17T07:20:34.732459Z</sub>\\n\\nRT-ICA Snapshot: feat: itsaplan as a WorkItemBackend provider over its REST API and MCP endpoint\\nDate: 2026-10-17\\nGoal: Establish whether Itsaplan can serve as the configured DH work-item provider while preserving the provider-neutral ownership and lifecycle contract.\\nConditions:\\n1. DH work-item lifecycle, identity, status, milestone, capability, and remote-provider ownership requirements are documented in source. | Status: AVAILABLE\\n2. Itsaplan work-item endpoints, identity format, list pagination, and authenticated permissions can be verified from its current OpenAPI/API source. | Status: DERIVABLE\\n3. Itsaplan support for DH logical plan and artifact content records, revision/conflict behavior, and bounded discovery can be verified from its current API source. | Status: DERIVABLE\\n4. The target deployment URL, supported Itsaplan version, credential provisioning and permission scope are selected for a future implementation. | Status: MISSING\\n5. A native milestone capability matching DHs numeric milestone contract is verified, or a human-approved unsupported behavior is recorded. | Status: DERIVABLE\\n6. Backend provider work is scoped independently from Itsaplan runner integration in #4143. | Status: AVAILABLE\\nAVAILABLE count: 2\\nDERIVABLE count: 3\\nMISSING count: 1\\nDecision: APPROVED-WITH-GAPS\\n</div>\\n\\n## Research\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-10-17T07:23:28.508937Z</sub>\\n\\n### Upstream snapshot and version caveat\\n- Primary-source snapshot: upstream `main` was commit [`1c861053`](https://github.com/croffasia/itsaplan/commit/1c8610530b8ae6a89a69ac58e18b07fdc2efd523) when researched. GitHub tags identify [`v1.5.0`](https://github.com/croffasia/itsaplan/releases/tag/v1.5.0) at `6e0dc0b`; `main` is newer. Treat all source findings as main-at-snapshot, not as a guaranteed deployed release surface.\\n\\n### Verified REST and OpenAPI surface\\n- [`apps/api/src/app.ts`](https://github.com/croffasia/itsaplan/blob/1c8610530b8ae6a89a69ac58e18b07fdc2efd523/apps/api/src/app.ts) mounts public Scalar docs at `/docs` and a generated OpenAPI document at `/docs/json`; the document is generated from route TypeBox schemas. It documents `x-api-key` authentication, project refs as `<team>.<KEY>`, and an instance-configured API origin.\\n- [`modules/issues/index.ts`](https://github.com/croffasia/itsaplan/blob/1c8610530b8ae6a89a69ac58e18b07fdc2efd523/apps/api/src/modules/issues/index.ts) implements issue creation (`POST /projects/:projectKey/issues`), filtered list/search, reads by numeric id or project sequence, patch, archive/restore, delete, comments, checklists, fields, watchers, worklogs, activity and cycle history. The returned work-item schema includes identifiers, project/column/type, title/description, labels/custom fields, priority, estimates/dates, assignee/delegate user IDs, initiative/cycle, parent, archive state, and full reads add links, watchers, parent/subtasks, checklists and development links ([`model.ts`](https://github.com/croffasia/itsaplan/blob/1c8610530b8ae6a89a69ac58e18b07fdc2efd523/apps/api/src/modules/issues/model.ts)).\\n- REST authorization is route-level: issue operations declare `work_items` read/create/edit/delete permissions; full reads additionally invoke the project MCP toggle. The OpenAPI app description states that a personal `x-api-key` carries its owner permissions.\\n\\n### Verified MCP availability and authorization\\n- [`mcp/mount.ts`](https://github.com/croffasia/itsaplan/blob/1c8610530b8ae6a89a69ac58e18b07fdc2efd523/apps/api/src/mcp/mount.ts) mounts Streamable HTTP JSON-RPC at `POST /mcp`. It accepts `Authorization: Bearer` or `x-api-key`, first resolving a personal API key and otherwise an MCP OAuth access token; deactivated accounts are refused.\\n- [`mcp/generate.ts`](https://github.com/croffasia/itsaplan/blob/1c8610530b8ae6a89a69ac58e18b07fdc2efd523/apps/api/src/mcp/generate.ts) derives MCP tools only from REST routes marked `x-mcp`, then dispatches calls through the same route validation, permission guards and error model. The issue routes explicitly mark `create_issue`, `list_issues`, `search_issues`, `get_issue`, `get_issue_by_number`, `update_issue`, archive/restore/delete, link/unlink, comments and other operations.\\n- [`mcp/server.ts`](https://github.com/croffasia/itsaplan/blob/1c8610530b8ae6a89a69ac58e18b07fdc2efd523/apps/api/src/mcp/server.ts) resolves the callers team from its identity; a caller with multiple teams must supply `teamId` for team-scoped tools.\\n\\n### Identities and pagination\\n- `GET /me` and MCP `get_current_user` return the acting user and make `user.id` the value for ones own `assigneeUserId`; it also returns `isAgent` and timezone ([`modules/current-user/index.ts`](https://github.com/croffasia/itsaplan/blob/1c8610530b8ae6a89a69ac58e18b07fdc2efd523/apps/api/src/modules/current-user/index.ts)). Project member discovery is `GET /projects/:projectKey/members` / MCP `list_members`, with `kind` distinguishing people and AI agents ([`modules/members/index.ts`](https://github.com/croffasia/itsaplan/blob/1c8610530b8ae6a89a69ac58e18b07fdc2efd523/apps/api/src/modules/members/index.ts)).\\n- Standard paged routes use 1-based `page` and `pageSize` (default 25, maximum 100) and return `{ items, total, page, pageSize }` ([`shared/pagination.ts`](https://github.com/croffasia/itsaplan/blob/1c8610530b8ae6a89a69ac58e18b07fdc2efd523/apps/api/src/shared/pagination.ts)); member, initiative and completed-cycle routes use it. In contrast, issue list/search are array responses with `limit` default 50 and capped at 500; this source exposes no issue-list continuation token. Issue activity uses an opaque keyset `nextCursor`.\\n\\n### Relations, cycles, initiatives, milestones, and documents\\n- Work-item relationships are first-class: `POST /issues/:issueId/links` and its delete counterpart support blocks, blocked_by, relates, duplicates and duplicated_by; full issue reads include links. Parent/subtask links are fields on the issue schema.\\n- Cycles have list/get/create/update/delete/finish/transfer REST routes and MCP tools such as `list_cycles`, `get_cycle`, `create_cycle`, and `update_cycle` ([`modules/cycles/index.ts`](https://github.com/croffasia/itsaplan/blob/1c8610530b8ae6a89a69ac58e18b07fdc2efd523/apps/api/src/modules/cycles/index.ts)). Initiatives likewise have paged list, CRUD and MCP tools, and issue create/update accepts `initiativeId` ([`modules/initiatives/index.ts`](https://github.com/croffasia/itsaplan/blob/1c8610530b8ae6a89a69ac58e18b07fdc2efd523/apps/api/src/modules/initiatives/index.ts)).\\n- The recursive upstream tree and API tag list show no path containing `milestone`; `app.ts` also has no Milestones OpenAPI tag. This is an evidence-backed mapping gap, not proof that every deployed instance lacks a milestone feature.\\n- Documents are verified: list/get return visible Markdown content, and create/update, versioned revisions, archive/restore/delete, and explicit document-to-issue links are REST routes with corresponding MCP tools including `list_documents`, `get_document`, `create_document`, `update_document`, `link_document_issue`, and `list_issue_documents` ([`modules/documents/index.ts`](https://github.com/croffasia/itsaplan/blob/1c8610530b8ae6a89a69ac58e18b07fdc2efd523/apps/api/src/modules/documents/index.ts)). Asset upload/download exists as REST, but those asset routes are not marked `x-mcp` in this snapshot; no asset-tool mapping is verified.\\n\\n### Unverified requirements\\n- A target instance must expose `/docs/json` and `POST /mcp` and must be checked with OpenAPI plus MCP `tools/list`; source capability does not establish its configured version, enabled project features, permissions, or MCP toggle.\\n- Milestone mapping, issue-list traversal beyond the 500-result cap, and MCP document-asset operations are unverified from the observed upstream source.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Offers\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nresearch/task-management/itsaplan.md, \\\"Key Features > Platform\\\" and \\\"Problem Addressed\\\": a self-hosted tracker exposing a REST API with an OpenAPI reference and API keys, and an MCP endpoint at `POST /mcp` (Bearer or `x-api-key` auth). The entry states: \\\"REST API with an OpenAPI reference and API keys.\\\" and \\\"MCP endpoint at `POST /mcp`.\\\" It also documents an extension point: \\\"any API route can be exposed by adding an `x-mcp` extension to its OpenAPI detail\\\" (entry, Technical Architecture, Extension points).\\n</div>\\n\\n## Evidence\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- Read: `research/task-management/itsaplan.md` lines 36-64 (Platform list) and 92-96 (Extension points).\\n- Read: `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/backend_types.py` lines 175-214.\\n- Read: `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/backend_protocol.py` lines 170-182.\\n- Grep `backend\\\\.name|_VALID_BACKENDS|class \\\\w+(Backend|Provider)` in `plugins/development-harness`: `_VALID_BACKENDS` is the only tuple of backend family names.\\n- GitHub issue search `repo:Jamie-BitFlight/claude_skills itsaplan`: 0 results.\\n- GitHub issue search `repo:Jamie-BitFlight/claude_skills backend tracker Linear GitLab new backend WorkItemBackend`: #1177, #3262.\\n- Filing route: backlog MCP `backlog_add` failed (see ROUTE_FAILURES); filed through GitHub MCP `issue_write`.\\n- Semantic search tools (ccc, graphify) were not run in this scan. Grep and Glob were the search tools used.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Could Change\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nA new backend family, `itsaplan`, implementing `WorkItemBackend` over the itsaplan REST API or its MCP endpoint, so that the dh backlog MCP server reads and writes work items in a self-hosted tracker instead of GitHub Issues. Setup cost: a running itsaplan instance (entry, Installation: Docker and Bun, PostgreSQL, api/worker/web services), an API key, and a `create_backend` branch plus a `_VALID_BACKENDS` entry. `WorkItemBackend` requires milestone create, list and assign methods on every backend; `backend_types.py:199-207` documents the `supports_milestones` flag and the `NotImplementedError` escape hatch. The entry lists no milestone concept among its features, so mapping milestones is a required check before implementation.\\n\\nRelated open issues, not duplicates: #1177 (formalise an adapter Protocol for GitLab and Linear), #3262 (WorkItemBackend method names are GitHub-specific).\\n</div>\\n\\n## Touches\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nThe dh backlog backend contract. `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/backend_types.py:182` defines `class WorkItemBackend(Protocol)`, documented as \\\"Generic work-item surface every backend must implement\\\". `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/backend_protocol.py:176` sets `_VALID_BACKENDS: tuple[str, ...] = (\\\"github\\\", \\\"memory\\\", \\\"sqlite\\\", \\\"beads\\\")`. The factory `create_backend` at `backend_protocol.py:179` dispatches on that name.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"b888186c164067ba304a0caf4068ac04ea8d7d1cc8660f522226ed343de3a9b8\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABc2g1bw\",\"fields\":{\"files\":\"\",\"priority\":\"P2\",\"close_comment\":\"\",\"language\":\"\",\"added\":\"2026-10-17\",\"item_type\":\"Feature\",\"status\":\"needs-grooming\",\"close_reason\":\"\",\"stack\":\"\",\"topic\":\"\",\"source\":\"Not specified\",\"groomed\":\"2026-10-17\",\"layer\":\"\",\"followup_to\":\"\",\"plan\":\"\",\"close_reference\":\"\",\"suggested_location\":\"\",\"research_first\":\"\"}}"}